From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm-dai: allow 5 ms playback periods

q6apm-dai makes every period and buffer a multiple of 480 frames (10 ms
at 48 kHz), for playback and capture alike. A user space that writes
5 ms blocks and keeps three periods queued still gets 3 x 480 frames,
so the ALSA buffer alone holds up to 30 ms of audio. On gaokun3 this is
the largest part of the output latency of games.

The SC8280XP ADSP does not need 10 ms playback periods. With 3 x 240
frames, rhythm game sessions played without audible gaps, and the
output timestamps still matched an acoustic loopback measurement. What
the DSP does need is more than two periods queued: 2 x 480 frames gaps
audibly. The DSP then holds on to its last period and ALSA raises no
XRUN, so nothing in the driver can see it; user space has to keep at
least three periods.

Use a 240-frame step for playback. Capture keeps the 480-frame step.
The step applies to every playback front end. Both gaokun3 playback
paths were tested: the speaker (WSA codec DMA, fed by MultiMedia2) and
wired headphones (RX codec DMA, fed by MultiMedia1).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [tested only with the SC8280XP ADSP firmware]
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
index 8b23cd911..b9c729883 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
@@ -28,6 +28,13 @@
 #define CAPTURE_MAX_NUM_PERIODS		8
 #define CAPTURE_MAX_PERIOD_SIZE		65536
 #define CAPTURE_MIN_PERIOD_SIZE		6144
+/*
+ * Period and buffer sizes are multiples of this many frames. The SC8280XP
+ * ADSP plays 5 ms periods without gaps when user space keeps three or more
+ * of them queued; capture keeps the original 10 ms step.
+ */
+#define PLAYBACK_PERIOD_STEP		240
+#define CAPTURE_PERIOD_STEP		480
 #define BUFFER_BYTES_MAX (PLAYBACK_MAX_NUM_PERIODS * PLAYBACK_MAX_PERIOD_SIZE)
 #define BUFFER_BYTES_MIN (PLAYBACK_MIN_NUM_PERIODS * PLAYBACK_MIN_PERIOD_SIZE)
 #define COMPR_PLAYBACK_MAX_FRAGMENT_SIZE (128 * 1024)
@@ -387,6 +394,7 @@ static int q6apm_dai_open(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	struct q6apm_dai_data *pdata;
 	struct q6apm_dai_rtd *prtd;
 	int graph_id, ret;
+	unsigned int step;
 
 	graph_id = cpu_dai->driver->id;
 
@@ -430,14 +438,16 @@ static int q6apm_dai_open(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 		}
 	}
 
-	/* setup 10ms latency to accommodate DSP restrictions */
-	ret = snd_pcm_hw_constraint_step(runtime, 0, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_PERIOD_SIZE, 480);
+	/* period step to accommodate DSP restrictions */
+	step = substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK ?
+	       PLAYBACK_PERIOD_STEP : CAPTURE_PERIOD_STEP;
+	ret = snd_pcm_hw_constraint_step(runtime, 0, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_PERIOD_SIZE, step);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(dev, "constraint for period bytes step ret = %d\n", ret);
 		goto err;
 	}
 
-	ret = snd_pcm_hw_constraint_step(runtime, 0, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_BUFFER_SIZE, 480);
+	ret = snd_pcm_hw_constraint_step(runtime, 0, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_BUFFER_SIZE, step);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(dev, "constraint for buffer bytes step ret = %d\n", ret);
 		goto err;
